From 5650bbc152110fc5318a06d1b7d8ee2c70d4d807 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <226450061+logdog2325@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 15:34:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] XD Netplay v1.7.5: out-of-sync warning, GBA start check,
 focus notice and steadier input buffer

Out-of-sync warning. Each machine in an XD room reports two things to the
host. Inputs: every 240 pops of the first mapped pad (about 2 s), a hash of
the pad entries it consumed since its last report (every pad, in pop
order, only the fields that travel on the wire), tagged with the pop count.
XD state: a digest of XD's battle state read at every 256th GC->GBA WRITE
of each GBA port, tagged with that WRITE count (the wseq of the xd lines).
The WRITE is the game's own store, so every machine reads the same point
in the game even when x86 and ARM split their JIT blocks differently,
which a pad pop cannot promise. The host compares the players' reports per
tag. An inputs difference is announced at once; an XD difference only when
two tags of the same port in a row differ, and a single one is logged as
'statesync xd-transient'. On the first announced mismatch of a game every
machine logs 'statesync mismatch' with the part that differs (inputs, xd)
and the tag, and the room chat says "Out of sync since HH:MM:SS. Restart
the battle." The line goes to the room chat only, never on screen, and is
repeated once in the chat when the game stops. A spectator whose report
differs from the players' is logged everywhere and told alone ("Your view
of the battle is out of sync since HH:MM:SS."). Warn only; nothing stops
the game. Each game's log says 'statesync on' or 'statesync off' with the
reason (not XD, host input authority). Nothing is read from the GBA cores.

crcB in the xd lines was always 0: the context cell holds a trainer's
active slot, not the context base. The base is now recovered from it, so
the lines carry a real party/HP checksum.

A GBA core that fails to start under netplay now stops the game for
everyone with one room chat line; a spectator's failure stops only that
spectator. Solo is unchanged.

Timing holes: Import Save / Restore Default and Boot Solo are refused while
a room is open, XD Start waits until the previous game has fully closed
and is refused with RetroAchievements hardcore on, and the boot log gets
'onframe active' and 'gecko active' fingerprint lines next to 'ar active'.

Focus notice: after 5 s with the game window out of focus or the game
paused (Pause on Focus Loss, the pause button, or Android leaving the game
screen), the room chat says "<name> left the game window.", and "<name> is
back in the game window." on return. Rate-limited, chat only, never on
screen.

Input buffer: players report once a second, over the pads other machines
own, their waits and the smallest queue depth seen before a pop. The
automatic buffer lowers only while every player keeps at least 3 entries
of slack, and when a player waits on at least half of those pops with an
empty queue for 3 s in a row it adds 4 entries (at most 12 over the ping
target, never past 20). Every raise re-anchors the throttle so the new
slack is kept. Only when entries are sent changes, never which.
